=== full tail of one RED run (the terminating fault, shown once) ===
--- obj_dir_tb_matvec_red/tb_matvec_red --seed 1 +vecdir=vecv2/w11_w8
[633000] FAIL: row 22: y32=fffe2298 golden=ffe82ccc
[200000000000] %Fatal: tb_matvec.sv:379: Assertion failed in TOP.tb_matvec: TB_MATVEC FAIL: global watchdog
%Error: tb_matvec.sv:379: Verilog $stop
Aborting...
timeout: the monitored command dumped core
rc=134 (SIGABRT from $fatal)

Every row of every W8 shape/seed is wrong and the stream never completes:
HEAD's engine consumes cfg_ng+scale beats per row (2 or 5 here) while the
W8 image supplies 2*cfg_ng+scale (3 or 9), so the input side runs dry and
the 200 ms watchdog is what ends the run.  This is the RED the W8 mode fixes.
